  "title": "bus.reindex(): add an index row for every task JSON that has none; daemon calls it at start",
  "spec": "Why: on 2026-09-30 luna T-0556 and T-0557 had task files but no sqlite row; bus.read (bus.py:200) lists only indexed tasks, so dispatch never saw them for a day (gotchas.md 2026-09-30).\nWhat: bus.reindex() -> {\"added\": [ids], \"skipped\": [{\"file\", \"error\"}]}: under locked(), for every tasks/T-*.json whose stem has no row, load it and _save it (which inserts the row); unparseable files are skipped with the error text. Do not rewrite rows that exist. Wiring into daemon start is task C6; this task only adds the function and its test.\n\nWork on the task branch cut from goal/T-1403. Commit first, then run the focused acceptance test in the foreground (uv run python -m pytest <id> -q). Never background a command and never run the full gate; the daemon gates externally. Acceptance ids are tests/<file>.py::<function or method name>; write the test as a unittest.TestCase method using tests/_harness.py like the neighbouring tests.",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_bus.py::test_reindex_adds_missing_json_rows passes: a task JSON written without an index row is invisible to bus.read(status=...), reindex() returns its id, and afterwards bus.read(status='queued', role='execute') returns it; an unparseable JSON file is skipped and reported, not raised",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh wt/THIS-TASK exits 0"
  ],
  "scope": [
    "orchestrator/bus.py",
    "tests/test_bus.py"
  ],
